{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"nosy-sunbeamy-monkey","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\nDuring the 2026-09-07 rotation (auspicial-wily-warbler), SSM was treated as the single point of rotation, but two GitHub Actions repo secrets mirroring SSM values went stale: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY and JIRA_API_TOKEN kept their 2026-08-12 values until manually synced on 2026-09-08. Workflows reference: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, GERRIT_SSH_PRIVKEY, JIRA_API_TOKEN, OPENAI_API_KEY, REBAR_BOT_SIGNING_KEY (+ JIRA_URL/JIRA_USER non-secrets). Any secret that lives in BOTH SSM and GitHub Actions must be rotated in both, or CI fails with stale credentials after the old value is revoked.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A documented inventory maps each GitHub Actions secret to its SSM source (or marks it GitHub-only), in the ops runbook that owns rotation (infra/runbooks/).\n- [ ] The rotation runbook includes an explicit GitHub Actions sync step (gh secret set from SSM) with a copy-paste command per mapped secret.\n- [ ] Optional (evaluate): a drift check that compares gh secret updated_at against SSM parameter LastModifiedDate and flags mirrors older than their source, surfaced through an existing operational channel (no new CI-provider-only mechanism; must have an operation-linked or in-process fallback per project.portability).\n\n## Verification\n- Runbook review: rotating any mapped secret following the runbook leaves no stale mirror.","id":"f116-c8d0-1e69-4361","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Secret-rotation procedure must include GitHub Actions secret sync"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788839556194303001,"uuid":"73c24e54-2c8d-454f-b7d2-953e71f7b06d"}